# Test: an operator-configured per-MAC session cap admits one session from a
# MAC and refuses a second, distinct session from that same MAC, and the
# refusal is visible on the operator's own metrics endpoint.
#
# VALIDATES: RFC 2516 places no per-peer session limit (rfc/short/rfc2516.md),
#            so a MAC below the cap gets a normal PADS with a non-zero
#            session id for its first session (server.go, handlePADR)
# VALIDATES: a second, genuinely distinct session from the same MAC (its own
#            PADI/PADO round trip, so its own AC-Cookie) gets a PADS carrying
#            an AC-System-Error tag and session id 0x0000 once the MAC is at
#            max-sessions-per-mac (server.go, admitPerMACCap, TagACSystemError)
# VALIDATES: the refusal increments ze_pppoe_discovery_refusals_total{reason=
#            "per-mac-cap-reached"}, readable on the operator's own Prometheus
#            endpoint (metrics.go, countRefusal)
# PREVENTS: an AC that keeps allocating a fresh session ID, AF_PPPOX socket,
#           and /dev/ppp channel and unit every time one MAC's PADR admits --
#           delete the admitPerMACCap call in handlePADR
#           (internal/component/l2tp/pppoe/server.go) and the second session
#           below gets admitted instead of refused
#           (spec-pppoe-padr-replay-allocates-unbounded-sessions, AC-1).
option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,net-raw
option=netns-link:name=veth-bng:peer=veth-sub


stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
pppoe {
    enabled true
    ac-name ze-test
    max-sessions-per-mac 1
    interface veth-bng {
    }
}

telemetry {
    prometheus {
        enabled true
        server main {
            ip 127.0.0.1
            port $PORT2
        }
    }
}
EOF_CONF

option=env:var=ze.log.pppoe:value=debug
option=env:var=TEST_IFACE:value=veth-sub

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=config
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze-test fixture pppoe/per-mac-cap:timeout=45s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: first session admitted, session-id=
expect=stdout:contains=OK: second session from the same MAC refused at the per-MAC cap

# The operator's own read-back: the refusal above must be counted, by the
# label an operator would filter on, not merely logged.
http=wait:seq=1:url=http://127.0.0.1:$PORT2/metrics:status=200:contains=ze_pppoe_discovery_refusals_total{reason="per-mac-cap-reached"} 1:timeout=30s
